# RPC contract

This page is the canonical wire contract for public PokerLost RPC operations implemented by
`{{ service_name }}`.

## System boundary

`GET /` is the sole non-RPC path. `GET /openapi.get` is the platform OpenAPI publication operation.
The `pypokerlost` generator treats both as system paths and does not generate callable methods for
them.

Every added public service operation has a lowercase namespace and method:

```text
operation_id = lowercase namespace.method
path         = "/" + operation_id
```

The complete accepted operation pattern is:

```text
^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*(?:\.[a-z][a-z0-9_]*)+$
```

Define one module-level `OPERATION` constant and derive both `path` and `operation_id` from it. The
SDK-compatible HTTP methods are `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, and `DELETE`; use `POST` by default
unless the operation semantics require another supported method.

## Request body

Application input is one named, closed, typed JSON object based on `RequestModel`. Its component and
class name ends in `Request`. Application-owned field names are alias-free `snake_case` and remain
unchanged during serialization.

RPC application input does not use OpenAPI path, query, header, or cookie parameters. Do not use an
embedded body, an anonymous inline object, or a free-form top-level body. A `GET` operation that has
input still receives a JSON body. A parameterless operation omits `requestBody` completely instead
of publishing an empty object.

## Response schemas

A successful operation publishes `ApplicationResponse[<SemanticName>Response]`. Every expected
handled 4xx or 5xx response publishes `ApplicationResponse[None]`; an operation with a request body
also publishes that model for validation status `422`. All numeric 2xx responses for one operation
must use compatible JSON schemas.

The envelope fields and invariants belong to
[ApplicationResponse](application-response.md), and runtime failure mappings belong to
[API errors](errors.md).

## Service-specific security

When a concrete service requires authorization, declare it through that service's FastAPI security
dependencies. It must not alter the operation, path, application-input, or response-envelope rules.
FastAPI-generated security metadata remains service-specific and is preserved by the
[OpenAPI publication](openapi-and-sdk.md).

## Contract changes

An API change must update the [public surface manifest](public-surface.md), this page when the RPC
rules change, and the relevant response or publication page. A wire-contract change also requires
the authoritative `pypokerlost` compatibility workflow.
